   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`delete INDEX` now works, and the project checks pass.\n\n**Red run:** before the implementation, 4 of the 5 tests failed. Two failed with `AttributeError: module 'fieldnotes.store' has no attribute 'delete'`, and two failed because the CLI returned exit code 2 for the unknown `delete` command. The existing `add`/`load` test still passed.\n\n**Green run:** `tools/check.py` ran 5 tests, all OK, and the line-length rule also passed (exit 0). I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointed at a scratch temp directory, since the script requires that variable.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `fieldnotes/store.py`: new `delete(index)` removes and returns the note at a 1-based index. It raises `IndexError` for 0, negative or too-large values and leaves the file untouched in that case.\n- `fieldnotes/cli.py`: new `delete INDEX` command that prints `deleted: <text>` and exits 0. A non-numeric or out-of-range index prints an error to stderr and exits 1. I also moved the usage message into one `USAGE` constant that now mentions `delete`.\n- `tests/test_store.py`: two store tests and two CLI tests for the command.\n\n**INDEX is 1-based, and `list` doesn't show indexes yet.** Users currently have to count lines to pick one. I left `list` alone to keep this change scoped. Numbering its output would be a small follow-up, but it changes the existing output format, so I didn't do it unasked.",
